From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:53:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] freedreno/a2xx: Xenos texture barrier inside the batch;
 cheaper blits and readback

- Texture barrier: a Xenos batch renders as one bin, so its draws run once,
  in order. Resolve the color buffer area drawn since the last barrier in the
  middle of the draw stream instead of flushing the batch. glamor calls
  glTextureBarrierNV before every copy within a pixmap. XENOS_FLUSH_BARRIER
  restores the flush.
- Blits without a scissor get their destination box as the scissor, so the
  batch restores and resolves only that box, and Xenos skips the post-blit
  flush of the destination's writer (GLES2: no stencil texturing).
- Blit every 32-bit texture transfer (texture_transfer_blit_min_pixels = 1,
  XENOS_BLIT_MIN_PIXELS overrides), and only when the client's pixels are
  4 bytes too: 16-bit formats sample wrongly from the staging texture.
- Readback staging of 64K or more is mapped cached; dcbf the mapped level
  before the CPU reads it.

x11perf: copywinwin10 7550 -> 15200, putimage10 5700 -> 16300,
putimage100 1070 -> 4870, getimage500 14 -> 62.

